### 7.7 Iterator Pattern

**Intent:** Provide a way to sequentially access elements of a collection without exposing its underlying structure.

```java
public interface Iterator<T> {
    boolean hasNext();
    T next();
}

public class NumberIterator implements Iterator<Integer> {
    private int[] numbers;
    private int index = 0;

    public NumberIterator(int[] numbers) { this.numbers = numbers; }
    public boolean hasNext() { return index < numbers.length; }
    public Integer next()    { return numbers[index++]; }
}
```

