## 8. UML Diagrams

### 8.1 Class Diagram Notations

```
+------------------+
|    ClassName     |   <-- Class Name
+------------------+
| - privateField   |   <-- Attributes (- private, + public, # protected)
| + publicField    |
+------------------+
| + publicMethod() |   <-- Methods
| - privateMethod()|
+------------------+
```

### 8.2 Relationships

| Relationship | Symbol | Meaning | Example |
|--------------|--------|---------|---------|
| **Association** | `——>` | A uses B | Student uses Library |
| **Aggregation** | `◇——>` | Weak has-a | Department has Employees |
| **Composition** | `◆——>` | Strong has-a (lifecycle) | House has Rooms |
| **Inheritance** | `——▷` | Is-a | Dog is an Animal |
| **Realization** | `- -▷` | Implements interface | List implements Iterable |
| **Dependency** | `- ->` | Uses temporarily | Order depends on Tax |

### 8.3 Cardinality

| Notation | Meaning |
|----------|---------|
| `1` | Exactly one |
| `0..1` | Zero or one |
| `*` or `0..*` | Zero or many |
| `1..*` | One or many |
| `2..5` | Between 2 and 5 |

### 8.4 Sequence Diagram Elements

```
Actor    Object1    Object2    Object3
  |          |          |          |
  |--msg1--> |          |          |   -- Synchronous call
  |          |--msg2--> |          |
  |          |          |--msg3--> |
  |          |          |<--ret3---|   -- Return
  |          |<--ret2---|          |
  |<--ret1---|          |          |
```

