## 12. LLD Interview Approach

### Step-by-Step Framework (45-minute interview)

#### Step 1: Clarify Requirements (3–5 min)

- What are the core entities/objects?
- What operations are needed?
- What are the constraints (concurrency, scale)?
- Any special behaviors (undo, notifications)?

#### Step 2: Identify Entities & Classes (5–7 min)

- List all nouns → candidate classes
- List all verbs → candidate methods
- Identify relationships

#### Step 3: Define Interfaces & Abstractions (5 min)

- What behaviors are shared across types? → Interfaces
- What state and behavior is shared? → Abstract classes

#### Step 4: Draw Class Diagram (10 min)

- Show classes, attributes, methods
- Show relationships (inheritance, composition, association)
- Indicate cardinalities

#### Step 5: Deep Dive Into Key Classes (10 min)

- Write out method signatures
- Discuss algorithms for complex operations
- Discuss data structures used internally

#### Step 6: Design Patterns (5 min)

- Identify which patterns apply
- Explain why you chose them

#### Step 7: Handle Edge Cases & Concurrency (5 min)

- Concurrent access issues
- Error scenarios
- Validation rules

### Common Mistakes to Avoid

| Mistake | Fix |
|---------|-----|
| Jumping to code without understanding requirements | Always ask clarifying questions first |
| Making everything public | Apply encapsulation; expose minimal interface |
| Using only inheritance | Prefer composition; use interfaces |
| Not using design patterns | Identify patterns naturally |
| Ignoring concurrency | Discuss thread safety for shared state |
| Over-engineering | Keep it simple; add complexity only when needed |
| Not validating inputs | Add input validation at boundaries |

